    "answer": {
      "short": "The error is accepting every candidate after squaring without checking the original equation. Reject $180^\\circ$ and $270^\\circ$, which give $-1$ rather than $1$. The solutions are $x=0^\\circ,90^\\circ,360^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Squaring allows $\\sin x+\\cos x=-1$ as well as $\\sin x+\\cos x=1$. The error is accepting every candidate without checking.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin0^\\circ+\\cos0^\\circ&=1\\\\\\sin90^\\circ+\\cos90^\\circ&=1\\\\\\sin180^\\circ+\\cos180^\\circ&=-1\\\\\\sin270^\\circ+\\cos270^\\circ&=-1\\\\\\sin360^\\circ+\\cos360^\\circ&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $x=0^\\circ,90^\\circ,360^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
